diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index 26b3bb6..a349c7e 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -2,9 +2,7 @@ Version 4.0.0 (2026-11-01)
 ==========================
 
 ``dateutil`` 4.0 requires Python 3.11 or later and no longer depends on
-``six``. Apart from that, the changes in this release are bug fixes, but note
-that ``isoparse`` is now stricter about the numeric fields it accepts (see
-below).
+``six``.
 
 
 Deprecations
@@ -15,31 +13,6 @@ Deprecations
   the public API, such as ``dateutil.tz.tzname_in_python2``. (gh pr #1625)
 
 
-Bugfixes
---------
-
-- ``parser.isoparse``, and the ``isoparser`` methods ``parse_isodate``,
-  ``parse_isotime`` and ``parse_tzstr``, now require each numeric field to be
-  exactly the expected number of ASCII digits. Strings that were previously
-  accepted, such as ``20200728121240`` (read as 21:24), ``2014- 4-21`` and
-  ``2_14-04-21``, and offsets such as ``+-1:00``, now raise ``ValueError``.
-  ``tzical`` applies the same check to ``TZOFFSETFROM`` and ``TZOFFSETTO``.
-  Reported by @janos-gonye (gh issue #1074). Fixed by @varun3257 (gh pr #1617).
-- Fixed an issue where iterating over a cached ``rrule`` or ``rruleset`` could
-  hang forever if another iterator over the same rule had already completed the
-  cache, for example when a cached ``rrule`` was included twice in an
-  ``rruleset``. Reported by @bysiber (gh pr #1455). Fixed by @pganssle (gh pr
-  #1655).
-- Unpickling a ``tzutc`` now gives the ``dateutil.tz.UTC`` singleton, and
-  unpickling a ``tzoffset`` gives the same object as calling
-  ``tzoffset(name, offset)``. Previously unpickling bypassed the
-  singleton-generation logic. Reported and fixed by @masipcat (gh issue #1051,
-  gh pr #1053).
-- ``relativedelta(yearday=366)`` now resolves to December 31 in leap years.
-  Previously it gave December 30, the same date as ``yearday=365``. Reported
-  and fixed by @Master-Norna (gh pr #1583).
-
-
 Misc
 ----
 
@@ -112,9 +85,6 @@ Bugfixes
   same time as a DST transition (e.g. in ``America/Bahia_Banderas`` in 2010).
   Against the standard offsets in the tz database source, the only remaining
   errors are in ``Europe/Paris`` in 1944 and 1945. (gh pr #1130)
-- Fixed ``rrulestr`` raising ``ValueError`` on experimental ``X-`` parameters in
-  an ``RRULE`` line (such as GNOME Evolution's ``X-EVOLUTION-ENDDATE``); these are
-  now ignored as RFC 5545 permits. Fixed by @yajo (gh pr #1374)
 - Enabled pickling and deepcopy of cached ``rrule`` and ``rruleset`` instances.
   The cache setting is preserved, and cached results are regenerated on demand
   without copying locks or generators. Reported by @niccokunzmann (gh issue #1369).
